title: How the hook works
description: claude/hook.mjs as a developer reads it, on the happy path — what the script defines and does, in order, and what it writes to stdout, in full. What can go wrong is hook-unhappy.playbook beside it.
sections:
  - title: 1 · Define the paths and the mode
    children:
      - title: Define DIR
        body: |
          Define `DIR` to be the folder the script sits in.
      - title: Define MASTER
        body: |
          Define `MASTER` to be `claude.playbook` in `DIR`.
      - title: Define MEMORY
        body: |
          Define `MEMORY` to be `memory.brief` in `DIR`.
      - title: Define mode
        body: |
          Define `mode` to be the argument the script was run with, `session` when there is none.
  - title: 2 · Load js-yaml
    body: |
      Define `yaml` to be js-yaml from filekinds' install under `packages/filekinds`.
  - title: 3 · Define eventName
    body: |
      Define `eventName` to be `UserPromptSubmit` when `mode` is `prompt`, `SessionStart`
      otherwise.
  - title: 4 · Load the master
    body: |
      Check that a file exists at `MASTER`. Read it as text and define `doc` to be that text
      parsed by `yaml` as one YAML document, whatever its shape.
  - title: 5 · Load the memory
    body: |
      Check that a file exists at `MEMORY`. Read it as text and define `memoryDoc` to be that
      text parsed by `yaml` as one YAML document, whatever its shape.
  - title: 6 · Define working and areas
    body: |
      Define `working` to be the `events` list of `doc`, and `areas` to be the `sections` list of
      `memoryDoc` — the memory's top sections, one per area, each with one child per fact.
  - title: 7 · Define lines
    body: |
      Define `lines` to be one line per event of `working`: the event's label, an arrow, and the
      names of its content entries — the one entry of a version-2 event, each entry of a
      version-1 event's list — separated by commas, or `(no content yet)` when it has none.

      ```
      - <event label> → <name of entry>, <name of entry>
      - <event label> → (no content yet)
      ```

      An entry's name: a file entry is named by its file, followed by ` by ` and its decisions
      when it varies (`steps.brief by push`); a written entry by its label — else its key, else
      `content` — and its kind in parentheses, `md` when none is given (`Updating content (md)`).
  - title: 8 · Gather the questions
    body: |
      Define `questions` to be one line per child playbook written under a master event that
      carries decisions. Go through every event of `working` and every content entry of the
      event — the one entry of a version-2 event, each entry of a version-1 event's list — and
      take the entry when its kind is `playbook` and it holds one document; a set of child books
      (`by` + `docs`) is passed over, a book nested inside a child is not walked, and the memory
      is not searched. A child with no decisions gives no line.

      ```
      <child's title> (under "<event label>"): <decision label> [<answer> / <answer>]; <decision label> [<answer> / <answer>]
      ```

      A missing child title is stood in for by the entry's label, else the event's; an answer is
      named by its label, else its key.
  - title: 9 · Split on the mode
    body: |
      What runs last follows `mode`.
    content:
      kind: playbook
      doc:
        version: 2
        title: What is written
        decisions:
          - key: mode
            label: Which argument was the script run with?
            values:
              - { key: prompt, label: prompt }
              - { key: session, label: session, anything else, or nothing }
        events:
          - key: write-prompt
            label: The mode is prompt
            trigger: imposed
            when: [mode=prompt]
            content:
              key: reminder
              label: Write the reminder
              kind: brief
              doc:
                title: Write the reminder
                sections:
                  - title: Write the reminder to stdout
                    body: |
                      Write this JSON to stdout, its text one paragraph with no line breaks.
                      `<event labels>` is every label of `working` joined by ` · `; `<areas>` is
                      the title of every section of `areas` — `(untitled)` for one without —
                      joined by `, `.

                      ```json
                      {"hookSpecificOutput": {"hookEventName": "UserPromptSubmit", "additionalContext": "Master playbook (<MASTER>): as you work, watch for these events and, when one happens, open its content in the book and do every item — <event labels>. MEMORY lives in <MEMORY>: before touching an area, take its section (<areas>) and read its facts. Never write to a book under claude/ except through the \"Something should be committed to memory\" event and Maher's answer there. The child books' questions have NO standing answer (a version-2 walk is session-only, nothing is ever saved): ask Maher each question in chat and act on his answer there; the event's content follows his answer, and until he answers the event's own hint says what to do."}}
                      ```

                      `questions`, the names of the events' content and the facts' titles are not
                      written.
                  - title: Exit 0
                    body: |
                      The script ends.
          - key: write-session
            label: The mode is session, anything else, or nothing
            trigger: imposed
            when: [mode=session]
            content:
              key: map
              label: Write the map
              kind: brief
              doc:
                title: Write the map
                sections:
                  - title: Write the map to stdout
                    body: |
                      Write this JSON to stdout, its text one string in which every line break
                      below is a newline. `<lines>` is `lines`, one per line; `<questions>` is
                      `questions`, each behind `- `, one per line, or the one line `- (no child
                      book carries a decision)`; `<memory lines>` is one line per section of
                      `areas` — its title, an arrow, and the titles of its children separated by
                      commas, `(untitled)` for a section or child without one.

                      ```json
                      {"hookSpecificOutput": {"hookEventName": "SessionStart", "additionalContext": "
                      MASTER PLAYBOOK — <MASTER> (version 2: every checklist and child book is in the file)
                      Consult it at the start of every task and whenever one of its events happens: open the event's content in the book and do every item. Maher adds events there in the Studio; keep the checklists true to how the Studio works; studio-check after editing.
                      <lines>
                      QUESTIONS — the child books' decisions. None has an answer in the file and nothing clicked in the Studio is saved: ask Maher each one in chat when its event fires; the event's content (docs, keyed by answer) is what to do under his answer, and the event's own hint is what to do until he answers.
                      <questions>
                      MEMORY — <MEMORY> (a brief, one file). Each top section IS Claude's memory for that area, one child per fact (there is no MEMORY.md). Take an area's section before working there and read its facts. Writing to memory.brief or to claude.playbook happens ONLY through the \"Something should be committed to memory\" event: show the write, ask, and write only on a yes; every write is shown in full in the report.
                      <memory lines>
                      "}}
                      ```
                  - title: Exit 0
                    body: |
                      The script ends.
